  "content": [
   {
    "text": "I labelled 1 column, but the file itself is not usable as-is and needs a re-read before the contract can be written.\n\nThe file is semicolon-delimited (`sniffed_delimiter: \";\"`), while the contract expects comma. So the whole header landed in a single column, and the profile names it `column_1`. I labelled that one entry `phi: true, role: other` because its contents include names, date of birth and patient reference.\n\nThe header it contains, in order, is: `member_id; first_name; last_name; dob; sex; plan_code; coverage_start; coverage_end; patient_ref`. Those nine fields are what the contract needs labelled. I could not label them individually because the profile only has `column_1`.\n\nNext step: re-read the file with delimiter `;` and profile again, so each field gets its own label. The drift cause looks like the delimiter change, though the vendor's member IDs may also not match the contract's `M` + 9 digits pattern (the shapes show `A999999999`). Those are worth checking when the contract is updated.",
    "type": "text"
   }
